    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d133-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d133-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Ford Library, NSC Institutional Files (H-Files), Box 68, NSDM 344.
                    Secret. Copies were sent to the Secretary of State, the Chairman of the JCS, and
                    the Director of the OMB. Scowcroft forwarded the draft NSDM to Ford under a
                    covering memorandum, January 13, with the recommendation that the President
                    approve it. Scowcroft’s memorandum noted that Ford had reviewed the NSC study on
                    U.S. Strategy and Naval Force Requirements (<ref target="#d110">Document
                        110</ref>) during the NSC meeting held on December 2, 1976, records of which
                    are <ref target="#d115">Documents 115</ref> and <ref target="#d116">116</ref>.
                    Scowcroft also wrote: “The attached draft NSDM describes the fundamental
                    rationale and content of your five-year shipbuilding program. The issuance of a
                    NSDM is appropriate because it completes the NSC review of the Navy shipbuilding
                    program and provides a decision document to establish formally your five-year
                    program.” (Ibid.)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d133-f2" n="2" xml:id="d133-f2-content">
